150.body:
git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/gustaleitcor/maestro
cd maestro
cp .env.example .env # the identity provider, MACHINE_SECRET, REDIS_URL
podman compose up --build -d The orq service stays up as the server. The view service builds maestro-view/dist and then exits. The reverse proxy serves that directory itself, with no container in between. On the page's host, the reverse proxy has two jobs. Send /api/* to orq on port 3005. This lets OIDC_REDIRECT_URL reach orq and makes the session cookie first-party. Serve maestro-view/dist for every other path. With Caddy: maestro.example.org { handle /api/* { reverse_proxy localhost:3005 } handle { root * /srv/maestro/maestro-view/dist try_files {path} /index.html file_server }
}

